From 0bea22ad70b696dd332d93f2e35c06c4f8daff91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:43:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shadow): let a canvas claim the jog click
 (canvas_takes_click)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A canvas UI receives the jog wheel, knobs, knob-touch and pad notes, but never
the jog CLICK: the click is the close gesture and is taken before the canvas's
onMidi runs. That leaves a canvas with no "enter" action at all, so anything
hierarchical — a directory browser, a drill-down list, a confirm step — cannot
be expressed as a canvas UI.

Add `canvas_takes_click: true` (alias `canvastakesclick`) on a canvas param.
When set, the click is not stolen and falls through to dispatchCanvasMidi like
every other CC, arriving in the module's onMidi as MoveMainButton with d2 > 0.
Declining to steal is the whole change; nothing else was needed to route it.

Opt-in rather than default because the click is being taken AWAY from the host
— a module has to ask for it, and modules that do not are unaffected.

BACK IS NEVER CLAIMABLE and always closes the canvas. That is what makes this
safe to opt into: however a module's own navigation behaves, there is always
one guaranteed way out, so a module cannot trap the user by taking the only
exit.

Applies to both the fullscreen canvas and the co-run canvas overlay, so a
module's navigation behaves the same in either context.

docs/MODULES.md documents the flag, the contract, and the Back guarantee.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XX8gDJhHpYErLEwJsV5jPm
